  "tutorialReset": "Reset the exercise",
  "tutorialBoardTitle": "The board",
  "tutorialBoardBody": "Dhamet is played on the 81 intersections of a 9 × 9 grid of lines, drawn like four alquerque boards. Diagonals only run through every other point, the \"wide\" points. The other, \"narrow\" points have no diagonal.",
  "tutorialPiecesTitle": "The pieces",
  "tutorialPiecesBody": "Each side has 40 pieces; only the central intersection is empty at the start. Traditionally one side plays with sticks and the other with camel-dung pellets: here the light pieces carry a stick and the dark ones a ring.",
  "tutorialMoveTitle": "Moving",
  "tutorialMoveBody": "A pawn moves one step to an empty intersection, straight or diagonally along a line. It never moves backwards or sideways. Move the white pawn forward.",
  "tutorialCaptureTitle": "Capturing",
  "tutorialCaptureBody": "You capture by jumping over a neighbouring enemy piece to the free intersection right behind it, in any direction, even backwards. Capturing is mandatory. Capture the black pawn.",
  "tutorialRafleTitle": "Multiple captures",
  "tutorialRafleBody": "If the pawn can capture again after a capture, it goes on: a multiple capture. Captured pieces are removed at once, and you must always play the sequence taking the most pieces. Play the five-piece capture.",
  "tutorialPromotionTitle": "Promotion",
  "tutorialPromotionBody": "A pawn that ends its move on the opponent's last row becomes a Sultan. Take the pawn to the last row.",
  "tutorialSultanTitle": "The Sultan",
  "tutorialSultanBody": "The Sultan moves any number of intersections along a line, forwards or backwards. It captures a piece at a distance if the intersection behind it is free. Capture the black pawn with the Sultan.",
  "tutorialVictoryTitle": "Winning",
  "tutorialVictoryBody": "You win by capturing all the opponent's pieces, or when the opponent cannot move. Capture the last black piece.",
  "tutorialSpecialTitle": "Special rules",
  "tutorialSpecialBody": "When several captures are possible, the longest is mandatory. Traditionally, an incomplete capture sequence can be \"blown\" by the opponent; here the app simply enforces the right move. A few rules still need confirmation and are configurable. Play the longest capture.",
